---
description: Component folders, PascalCase files, nested local components
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Component files and folders

- One React component per file.
- Each component lives in a same-named folder with a same-named PascalCase file:
  `UserGreeting/UserGreeting.tsx`.
- If component B is used only by component A, put B under
  `A/components/B/B.tsx`.
- Do not put multiple components in the same file.
- Non-component helpers used only by that component may stay in the same file without export.
- Shared components live under grouped roots:
  - `components/ui/` — Mantine wrappers (thin re-exports)
  - `components/providers/` — app providers
- Mantine primitives used in the app get a local wrapper on first use:
  `components/ui/Button/Button.tsx` with a thin re-export from `@mantine/core`.
  Feature code imports only `@/components/...`, never `@mantine/core` directly.

```text
components/
  ui/
    Button/
      Button.tsx
  providers/
    TelegramProvider/
      TelegramProvider.tsx

app/
  UserGreeting/
    UserGreeting.tsx
    components/
      UserName/
        UserName.tsx
```

```tsx
// BAD
import { Button } from '@mantine/core'
app/UserGreeting.tsx          // file without folder
app/UserName.tsx              // sibling of parent, not nested
components/Button/Button.tsx  // flat under components/

// GOOD
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button/Button'
app/UserGreeting/UserGreeting.tsx
app/UserGreeting/components/UserName/UserName.tsx
```
